        "original_id": "834a2a18-ea87-5dd8-9e77-dd5aee8ee554",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey, Ayakapı, Sultanahmet Meydanı\n- Buildings: Gül Mosque, Hippodrome of Constantinople\n- Religions/Institutions: Eastern Orthodox Church, mosque, Ottomans\n\nFacts:\n- The Gül Mosque in Istanbul, Turkey, is a former Eastern Orthodox church that was converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\n- Ayakapı contains the Gül Mosque, one of the most important surviving Byzantine buildings on Istanbul’s historical peninsula.\n- The former Hippodrome of Constantinople is today a square called Sultanahmet Meydanı in Istanbul, and only a few fragments of the original structure survive.",
